@page "/customer-portal/privacy"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@rendermode InteractiveServer
@layout CustomerPortalLayout

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - Customer Portal</PageTitle>

@* On the portal's page vocabulary — the `cpd` blocks the dashboard was built
   from; see the Page vocabulary section of customer-portal.css. `cpx` comes
   down from the shell. `cpd-note`, `cpd-prose` and `cpd-stamp` were written in
   that file for these two legal pages and had no caller until now — the pages
   were still wearing the *staff* `staff-dashboard staff-shell` chrome inside
   the portal layout.

   The policy text is unchanged. Only the markup carrying it is: MudPaper and
   the MudText-per-paragraph stack became a panel of ordinary prose, which is
   what `cpd-prose` exists to set. *@
<div class="cpd fade-in">
    <div class="cpd-hero">
        <div class="cpd-hero-text">
            <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
            <div class="cpd-hero-meta">
                <span>How we collect, use and protect your information</span>
                <span>Last updated March 2026</span>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="cpd-hero-actions">
            <a href="/customer-portal/terms" class="btn btn-outline-primary">Terms of service</a>
            <a href="/customer-portal/support" class="btn btn-primary">Contact support</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="cpd-note">
        <i class="ph ph-info" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span>
            This Privacy Policy is issued in compliance with the Cyber and Data Protection Act
            [Chapter 12:07] of Zimbabwe and the regulations of the Postal and Telecommunications
            Regulatory Authority of Zimbabwe (POTRAZ).
        </span>
    </div>

    <div class="cpd-panel">
        <div class="cpd-stamp">Last updated: March 2026</div>

        <div class="cpd-prose">
            <h3>1. Data Controller</h3>
            <p>
                Kefalos Cheese (Pvt) Ltd is the data controller responsible for the personal data collected through
                this Customer Portal, as defined under the Cyber and Data Protection Act [Chapter 12:07]. We are
                registered with the Data Protection Authority of Zimbabwe as required by law.
            </p>

            <h3>2. Lawful Basis for Processing</h3>
            <p>
                In accordance with Section 8 of the Cyber and Data Protection Act, we process your personal data
                on the following lawful bases:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Consent:</strong> You have given consent for specific processing activities when
                    registering for and using this portal
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Contractual necessity:</strong> Processing is necessary to perform our contract with
                    you (invoicing, payments, statements)
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Legal obligation:</strong> Processing is required to comply with Zimbabwean law,
                    including tax and financial reporting requirements
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Legitimate interest:</strong> Processing is necessary for our legitimate business
                    interests, provided these do not override your fundamental rights
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>3. Information We Collect</h3>
            <p>We collect information you provide directly when using the Customer Portal, including:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Name, email address, phone number, and company details</li>
                <li>Billing information and payment details</li>
                <li>Transaction data related to invoices, payments, and statements</li>
                <li>Technical data such as IP address, browser type, and session information for security purposes</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>4. Purpose Limitation</h3>
            <p>
                In line with the data minimisation and purpose limitation principles under the Act, we use
                the information we collect only to:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Process and manage your invoices, payments, and account statements</li>
                <li>Communicate with you about your account and transactions</li>
                <li>Provide customer support and respond to your enquiries</li>
                <li>Improve our services and user experience</li>
                <li>Comply with legal and regulatory obligations, including POTRAZ requirements</li>
            </ul>

            <h3>5. Data Security</h3>
            <p>
                We implement appropriate technical and organisational measures to protect your personal data against
                unauthorised access, alteration, disclosure, or destruction, as required by the Cyber and Data
                Protection Act and POTRAZ security standards. All data transmitted between your browser and our
                servers is encrypted using TLS. Access to customer data is restricted to authorised personnel only.
                We conduct regular security assessments to ensure continued compliance.
            </p>

            <h3>6. Data Retention</h3>
            <p>
                We retain your personal data for as long as necessary to fulfil the purposes for which it was collected,
                including to satisfy legal, accounting, or reporting requirements under Zimbabwean law. Transaction
                records are retained in accordance with applicable financial regulations. When data is no longer
                required, it is securely deleted or anonymised in accordance with the Act.
            </p>

            <h3>7. Cross-Border Data Transfers</h3>
            <p>
                In accordance with Section 29 of the Cyber and Data Protection Act, we do not transfer your personal
                data outside Zimbabwe unless the receiving country provides an adequate level of data protection as
                determined by the Data Protection Authority, or appropriate safeguards are in place. Where cloud
                services are used, we ensure that data processing agreements meet the requirements of Zimbabwean law
                and POTRAZ regulations.
            </p>

            <h3>8. Third-Party Sharing</h3>
            <p>
                We do not sell your personal information to third parties. We may share your data with trusted service
                providers who assist us in operating the portal, processing payments, or complying with legal requirements.
                All third parties are contractually obligated to protect your data in accordance with the Cyber and Data
                Protection Act and are prohibited from using your data for any purpose other than the services they
                provide to us.
            </p>

            <h3>9. Your Rights as a Data Subject</h3>
            <p>Under Sections 22–28 of the Cyber and Data Protection Act, you have the following rights:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>
                    <strong>Right of access:</strong> Obtain confirmation of whether we process your personal data
                    and request a copy
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Right to rectification:</strong> Request correction of inaccurate or incomplete personal data
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Right to erasure:</strong> Request deletion of your personal data where there is no
                    compelling reason for continued processing
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Right to restriction:</strong> Request that we restrict the processing of your data in
                    certain circumstances
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Right to data portability:</strong> Receive your personal data in a structured, commonly
                    used, machine-readable format
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Right to object:</strong> Object to processing based on legitimate interests or for
                    direct marketing purposes
                </li>
                <li>
                    <strong>Right to withdraw consent:</strong> Withdraw your consent at any time without affecting
                    the lawfulness of processing carried out before withdrawal
                </li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                To exercise any of these rights, please contact us through the
                <a href="/customer-portal/support">Support</a> page.
                We will respond to your request within 30 days as required by law.
            </p>

            <h3>10. Data Breach Notification</h3>
            <p>
                In accordance with Section 30 of the Cyber and Data Protection Act, in the event of a personal data
                breach that is likely to result in a risk to your rights and freedoms, we will notify the Data
                Protection Authority within 72 hours of becoming aware of the breach. Where the breach is likely
                to result in a high risk to you, we will notify you directly without undue delay, providing details
                of the nature of the breach and the measures taken to address it.
            </p>

            <h3>11. Cookies</h3>
            <p>
                The Customer Portal uses essential cookies to maintain your session and preferences. These cookies are
                necessary for the portal to function and cannot be disabled. We do not use tracking or advertising cookies.
            </p>

            <h3>12. Complaints</h3>
            <p>If you believe your data protection rights have been violated, you have the right to:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>Contact us directly through the <a href="/customer-portal/support">Support</a> page</li>
                <li>
                    Lodge a complaint with the Data Protection Authority of Zimbabwe established under the Cyber
                    and Data Protection Act
                </li>
                <li>
                    Escalate regulatory matters to POTRAZ at
                    <a href="https://www.potraz.gov.zw" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.potraz.gov.zw</a>
                </li>
            </ul>

            <h3>13. Changes to this Policy</h3>
            <p>
                We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or applicable
                law. Material changes will be communicated to you via the portal or email. The "Last updated" date
                at the top of this policy indicates when the latest revision was made.
            </p>

            <h3>14. Contact Us</h3>
            <p>
                If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, wish to exercise your data rights, or need to
                report a data protection concern, please contact us through the
                <a href="/customer-portal/support">Support</a> page.
            </p>
            <p class="cpd-stamp">
                Regulatory enquiries may be directed to POTRAZ at
                <a href="https://www.potraz.gov.zw" target="_blank" rel="noopener">www.potraz.gov.zw</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
